{"abstract":"This timeline collects landmarks and events to present an overview of Danish digital game development. It showcases the formation of Danish game development from early grassroot networks and state inquiries to, among other things, the Law of NIMBI GameLab - Denmark's Institute for Game Development coming into effect in 2025.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Poulsen, Mark Staun","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-860980"],"filters":{"added":"2026-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danish game industry","History","Interest representation","Legislation","Policy","Timeline"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish game industry timeline","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/113877239/DanishGameIndustryTimelineImage.png","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-860980","ids":["itu-5d1eba8c-5395-42b4-a3b6-0952752f994f"],"keyword":["Danish game industry","history","interest representation","legislation","policy","timeline"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E6304A5DBF96D6D2362DBD36C5DD090B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/113877239/DanishGameIndustryTimelineImage.png","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.gamestimeline.dk","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Staun","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"6826c79c-8024-4f3c-bebf-f07d51e8988b","name":"Poulsen, Mark Staun","orcid":"0009-0006-6649-8165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5d1eba8c-5395-42b4-a3b6-0952752f994f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Danish Game Industry Timeline","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-860980","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"If politicians and game industry leaders are to be trusted, the Danish game industry is approaching a “new heyday” (Games Denmark 2024). The goal of this paper is to look closer into claims and hopes, occasional and sometimes hidden worries, about the future of Danish games. The material used consists of 1) reports, articles, and talks that address the future of the Danish games industry published in 2022-2024, and 2) analysis of 20 semi-structured interviews with Danish game developers working in small companies and having financial responsibilities of game development. Contrasting the strategically voiced ‘official' hopes and worries with circumstantial accounts of individual game workers, the paper reveals discrepancies between macro level ambitions on behalf of an industry and micro level anticipations and strategies for adopting game worker livelihood. The findings also highlight unique social contingencies underlying Danish game development culture and industrialization.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Poulsen, Mark Staun","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-860863"],"event":{"end":"2025-05-28","place":"Turku, fi","start":"2025-05-26","title":"Nordic DiGRA 2025 HOPE","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2026-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anticipatory discourses","Danish game industry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish game industry futures anticipations of a new heyday","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/113800887/Poulsen_and_Wirman_-_Danish_Game_Industry_Futures_Anticipations_of_a_New_Heyday_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-860863","ids":["itu-0c872c90-15f4-44f5-bc93-8b7c58d7bd32"],"keyword":["Danish game industry","Dansk spilbranche","Game business","Game production","anticipatory discourses","spilforretning","spilproduktion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EF79B2AB4AADEE7A47586B4BB1C65F4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/113800887/Poulsen_and_Wirman_-_Danish_Game_Industry_Futures_Anticipations_of_a_New_Heyday_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Staun","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"6826c79c-8024-4f3c-bebf-f07d51e8988b","name":"Poulsen, Mark Staun","orcid":"0009-0006-6649-8165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0c872c90-15f4-44f5-bc93-8b7c58d7bd32"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Danish Game Industry Futures : Anticipations of a “New Heyday”","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-860863","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we discuss an ethnographic field study conducted with a single 8-person development team operating within an established indie game company located in Copenhagen, Denmark, to explore how members of a development team – in this case mainly programmers and designers – coordinate their design ideas and development processes. In a view that accepts “the heterogeneity of production logics within the games industry” (Kerr 2017,76), our study of a single company in Denmark contributes new insights on organized and managed team creativity by adding to this pool of varying forms of development. The paper inquires and develops a perspective to analyse collaborative game-making within a studio workplace. We explore two formats of game development team meetings, Sprint Reviews and Sprint Retrospectives, to understand the ways in which teams work together to balance ‘creative-rational tensions’ (Tschang 2007) between given expectations and deadlines as well as personal expressive interests.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Poulsen, Mark Staun","Wirman, Hanna Elina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759422"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case study","Collaboration","Ethnography","Game Development","Game design","game design praxeology","game production studies","studio studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creative rational tensions in game development a danish case study on team collaboration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26503/todigra.v7i1.2184","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759422","ids":["itu-d5be4233-417c-4a58-b563-a86176d4169c"],"keywo